"},{"DocComment":" path.push(r\"C:\\\");"},{"DocComment":" path.push(\"windows\");"},{"DocComment":" path.push(\"system32\");"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" path.set_extension(\"dll\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" However, [`push`] is best used for dynamic situations. This is a better way"},{"DocComment":" to do this when you know all of the components ahead of time:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::path::PathBuf;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let path: PathBuf = [r\"C:\\\", \"windows\", \"system32.dll\"].iter().collect();"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" We can still do better than this! Since these are all strings, we can use"},{"DocComment":" `From::from`:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::path::PathBuf;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let path = PathBuf::from(r\"C:\\windows\\system32.dll\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Which method works best depends on what kind of situation you're in."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Note that `PathBuf` does not always sanitize arguments, for example"},{"DocComment":" [`push`] allows paths built from strings which include separators:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::path::PathBuf;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut path = PathBuf::new();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" path.push(r\"C:\\\");"},{"DocComment":" path.push(\"windows\");"},{"DocComment":" path.push(r\"..\\otherdir\");"},{"DocComment":" path.push(\"system32\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The behavior of `PathBuf` may be changed to a panic on such inputs"},{"DocComment":" in the future. [`Extend::extend`] should be used to add multi-part paths."}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"PathBuf"},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"r